{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Next batch evidence checkpoint\n\nUpdated the documentation worktree to origin/main at df8582f6e53c. The transient fetch race already has open bug agrologic-oval-bobolink, so no duplicate was created. GitHub metadata readback shows that aimless-seclusive-tigershark already installed the approved plan-review description. The current description matches that ticket, and repository topics remain unset. The completed description change will not be proposed again.\n\nCurrent main supports bounded candidates for operation-certificate guidance, required Jira project guidance, superseded Jira onboarding reference removal, Jira pressure-test entry points, connector-limited post-import validation, public mutation docstrings, mirror-lock runbook correction, concurrency source citations, Jira backend comments, MCP authentication module guidance, the SSO runbook link, Gerrit two-vote operations, third-party wordlist license packaging, and Jira Data Center Dockerfile provenance. Broad release-note, archive, prompt, experiment, comment, and runbook rewrites remain held because they lack a complete destination map or a bounded accuracy contract. F05 remains deferred. F23 and the lower README rewrite remain held. F02, F03, and F04 remain rejected.\n\nThe CLI-help correction ticket alamode-greasy-jerboa is in progress in another worktree. It is excluded from this batch while active. Any retained design must remove character-based absence assertions and use semantic wording, generator drift, and editorial review only. No recommendation will add mechanical prose or character enforcement.\n\nThe example-skill name proposal is rejected as unsupported. The existing checker and ticket db04-4d8b-cb4b-4114